From ba77a97d07597538e636b3cb3d5cae0d9c3e57c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lane <lane@local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 01:43:03 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 19/29] fix(executor): restore the missing brace that closed
 the non-MRT else branch

The merge from lanes/integ4 (a6470d4) brought in 6963b95's iteration-
group wiring, which is unbuildable as committed: GraphExecutor::execute()
fails -fsyntax-only with "expected expression" at the first `} catch
(const GraphError&`, cascading into "expected catch" and a final
"expected '}'" at the namespace close. This is not a merge artifact --
the identical byte-for-byte file at integ4's own 8c72107 fails the exact
same way when compiled directly against integ4's own include tree with
integ4's own flags (confirmed before touching anything: `diff -rq` shows
pysuite's and integ4's src/ and include/ trees are 100% identical after
the merge, and integ4's own executor.cpp reproduces the identical three
errors standalone). integ4-build's already-linked libnoisemaker-cpu.a
must predate whatever composed this exact text; the 6963b95 commit
message's own verification claims ("ctest: same two pre-existing
failures... 6 new tests all pass") don't match what this file compiles
to today.

Root cause: raw brace count over the whole file was 618 `{` vs 617 `}`
-- one short. Tracing nesting depth by hand through the pass-execution
try block (GraphExecutor::execute(), the MRT-vs-ordinary
`if (admission.outputs.size() > 1U) { ... } else { ... }` at line 3340)
found it: the non-MRT `else` opened at line 3417 is never closed. Its
body resolves the destination texture format, then branches again on
`if (dispatch_scatter) { ... } else { ... }` (3452-3525) -- and that
inner if/else's own closing brace at 3525 was mistaken for closing the
outer 3417 `else` too, leaving the `try` from line 3339 one level short
by the time execution reaches `} catch (const GraphError& error)` at
3526.

Fix: add the one missing `}` after line 3525, closing the 3417 `else`
before the `catch` chain. Purely mechanical -- no braces moved, no
lines reordered, nothing renamed; this is the minimum edit that
restores the structure the commit message itself describes (MRT branch
/ non-MRT branch, with the scatter/ordinary split nested inside the
latter). Verified: raw brace count is now 618/618; `-fsyntax-only
-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Werror` is clean; full rebuild succeeds; the
native suite (noisemaker-cpu-tests, including the new
test_graph_iterated_execution.cpp and test_mrt_kernel_and_pass_runner.cpp
integ4 added) is 600/601 PASS, the lone failure being the pre-existing
oracles2-owned classic-noise oracle metadata SHA (unrelated, unchanged
by this fix).

This is graph/executor.cpp, not part of this lane's Python-test-suite
brief -- flagging for whoever owns the iteration-group feature to
confirm the fix matches their intent, since I can't verify the new
run_iterated_group path's actual behavior, only that the file now
parses and the full native suite (old and new tests alike) passes.

